<title>AUSTRALIA: Rugby union-All Blacks too strong for Australia.</title>
<headline>Rugby union-All Blacks too strong for Australia.</headline>
<byline>Robert Galvin</byline>
<dateline>MELBOURNE 1996-07-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Holders New Zealand clinched the Bledisloe Cup and put one hand on the Tri-Nations championship with a 33-18 victory over Australia on Saturday -- a performance described by coach John Hart as proof of his side's outstanding resolve and character.</p>
<p>Hart described the All Blacks' emphatic victory, coming only one week after their stirring comeback win against South Africa in the series opener, as a sensational team effort.</p>
</text>
